# Reef Point hard rules

- **Any ticker, one stack.** Trigger: `analyze TICKER end-to-end` or `/analyze-company TICKER`. Follow `full-company-analysis`. Do not invent a second SEC/DCF engine.
- **Never invent a filing number.** Revenue, shares, debt, dates, quotes come from `artifacts/{TICKER}/01-sec/` or a cited form/date/accession. Else `DATA_GAP` or `UNVERIFIED`.
- **`EDGAR_IDENTITY` required.** Format `Name email@domain.com`. Stop if missing. Prefer `scripts/edgar_pull.py`. Never WebFetch `sec.gov`.
- **Pin `hishel==0.1.3`** if EDGAR `FileStorage` breaks (1.1.x did on the IREN test).
- **No Zapier.** No Make, n8n, email-to-Drive. Decks and workbooks: local PPTX/xlsx → Google Drive conversion-on-upload.
- **Studio `slides-deck` / `gws` / jackchuka are not official.** Official deck is `pptx-to-google-slides`.
- **Rate after the football field.** Buy / Hold / Sell must match the field. Tape above every non-circular high + a live kill = Sell, not a courtesy Hold. User-stated direction wins if they assert one.
- **One diluted count.** If-converted `value_shares` on every published bar. Cover-share `$/sh` is not the official mid.
- **Circular bars weight 0.** Own EV ÷ own ARR (or empty peer set using the target multiple) may draw; they do not enter the blend.
- **Do not publish on auditor `FAIL`** without an explicit user override.
- **Earnings calls do not move the rating.**
- **X is optional tape.** Never block a name on X.
- **IREN is the worked example, not a template to copy.** Do not reuse IREN shares, ARR, WACC, or the Sell $28 call on another name.
- Label every note `Draft view — not investment advice.`
